    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "omitted from the system boundary of the GHG accounting if\r\nevidence of this is provided.\r\nIn line with the GHG Accounting Module v1.0, The Project\r\nmust:\r\nConsider all GHGs associated with SSRs, in alignment\r\nwith the United States Environmental Protection\r\nAgency’s definition of GHGs, which includes: carbon\r\ndioxide (CO ), methane (CH ), nitrous oxide (N 0) and\r\nfluorinated gasses such as hydrofluorocarbons (HFCs),\r\nperfluorocarbons (PFCs), sulfur hexafluoride (SF ) and\r\nnitrogen trifluoride (NF ). For CO stored, only CO shall\r\nbe included as part of the quantification.\r\nFor all other activities all GHGs must be considered. For\r\nexample, the release of CO , CH , and N O is expected\r\nduring diesel consumption;\r\nQuantify emissions in tonnes CO equivalent (t CO e)\r\nusing the 100-year Global Warming Potential (GWP) for\r\nthe GHG of interest, based on the most recent volume of\r\nthe IPCC Assessment Report (currently the Sixth\r\nAssessment Report); and\r\nConsider materiality of SSRs in line with Isometric\r\nrequirements.\r\n2 4 2\r\n6\r\n3 2 2\r\n2 4 2\r\n2 2\r\nProject Proponents may exclude SSRs where the total\r\nemissions for that SSR, and all excluded SSRs collectively,\r\nare expected to be negligible. Negligible SSRs are those\r\nwhich fall below a Materiality threshold based on\r\nenvironmental significance of < 1% of net CO e removals.\r\n7.1.1\r\nMateriality\r\n2\r\n03/02/2026, 10:56 Biochar Production and Storage v1.2 — Isometric\r\nhttps://registry.isometric.com/protocol/biochar/1.2 31/103"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "<IMAGE FOR PAGE: 31 / 103>"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "<PARSED TEXT FOR PAGE: 32 / 103>"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Project Proponents must follow the Materiality assessment\r\nrequirements set out in Section 5 of the GHG Accounting\r\nModule v1.0.\r\nThe baseline scenario for biochar projects assumes that the\r\nactivities associated with the biochar Project do not take\r\nplace and that any infrastructure associated with the\r\nbiochar Project is not built.\r\nCounterfactual storage assesses the CO that would have\r\nremained durable stored as biogenic carbon in the absence\r\nof The Project. This durably stored portion is ineligible for\r\ncrediting as it is not environmentally additional. The\r\ncounterfactual storage of all feedstocks must be quantified\r\naccording to the Biomass Feedstock Accounting Module\r\nv1.3.\r\nSee Section 3 of the Biomass Feedstock Accounting Module\r\nfor requirements.\r\n7.2\r\nBaseline\r\n2\r\n03/02/2026, 10:56 Biochar Production and Storage v1.2 — Isometric\r\nhttps://registry.isometric.com/protocol/biochar/1.2 32/103"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "<PARSED TEXT FOR PAGE: 33 / 103>"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "8.0\r\nNet CDR Calculation\r\nThe Reporting Period, RP, for biochar projects represents the\r\ninterval of time over which removals are calculated and\r\nreported for verification. The equations used to calculate net\r\nCO e removals will pertain to all GHG emissions and CO\r\nremovals occurring over a Reporting Period. In most cases,\r\nthe Reporting Period represents a timeframe covering a\r\ncomplete cycle of activities, including biomass feedstock\r\nsourcing, pyrolysis, biochar processing, and biochar storage.\r\nFor all storage pathways associated with biochar, it is\r\nnecessary to calculate the total carbon (as CO e) stored in\r\nthe biochar ( ). Guidelines for determining\r\nare provided in Section 8.3.1. These calculations depend on\r\nmethodologies outlined in the relevant Storage Module and\r\ntherefore must be applied in conjunction with the relevant\r\nstorage Module calculations.\r\nIn addition to quantification, an initial\r\ncharacterization is required to determine the amount of CO\r\ndurably removed through biochar production. The specific\r\nrequirements and methodologies for this assessment are\r\nprovided in the relevant Storage Module.\r\nGHG emission calculations must include all emissions\r\nrelated to the project activities that occur within the\r\nReporting Period. This includes: (a) any emissions\r\nassociated with project establishment allocated to the\r\nReporting Period (See Section 8.6.1) (b) any emissions that\r\noccur within the Reporting Period (See Section 8.6.2), (c) any\r\n8.1\r\nCalculation Approach and Reporting\r\nPeriod\r\n2 2\r\n2\r\nCbiochar Cbiochar\r\nCbiochar\r\n2\r\n03/02/2026, 10:56 Biochar Production and Storage v1.2 — Isometric\r\nhttps://registry.isometric.com/protocol/biochar/1.2 33/103"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "<PARSED TEXT FOR PAGE: 34 / 103>"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "anticipated emissions that would occur after the Reporting\r\nPeriod that have been allocated to the Reporting Period\r\n(See Section 8.6.3) and (d) leakage emissions that occur\r\noutside of the system boundary that are associated with the\r\nReporting Period (See Section 8.6.4).\r\nTotal net CO e removal is calculated for each Reporting\r\nPeriod, and is written hereafter as . The final\r\nnet CO e removal quantification must be conservatively\r\ndetermined, giving high confidence that at a minimum, the\r\nestimated amount of CO e was removed.\r\nIn line with the Isometric Standard, this Protocol requires\r\nthat Removal Credits are issued ex-post. Credits may be\r\nissued once CO has been durably stored in the identified\r\nstorage reservoir.\r\n2\r\nCO e2 Removal,RP\r\n2\r\n2\r\n2\r\nNet CO e removal for the production of biochar and its\r\ndurable storage for each Reporting Period, , can be\r\ncalculated by Equation 1.\r\n(Equation 1)\r\nWhere:\r\n- the total net CO e removal for the\r\nReporting Period, RP, in tonnes of CO e.\r\n- the total CO removed from the\r\natmosphere and stored as organic carbon in the\r\n8.2\r\nCalculation of CO₂eRemoval, RP\r\n2\r\nRP\r\nCO2eRemoval,RP = CO2eStored,RP − CO2eCounterfactual,RP − CO2eEmi\r\nCO e2 Removal,RP 2\r\n2\r\nCO e2 Stored,RP 2\r\n03/02/2026, 10:56 Biochar Production and Storage v1.2 — Isometric\r\nhttps://registry.isometric.com/protocol/biochar/1.2 34/103"
    },
